import json,pathlib,re
root=pathlib.Path('.')
r=json.load(open('audit-evidence/browser.json')); inv=json.load(open('audit-evidence/test-inventory.json')); cov=json.load(open('audit-evidence/coverage-summary.json'))
src=pathlib.Path('PrivKnife/src/app/app.routes.ts').read_text(); routes={}
for m in re.finditer(r"path: '(tools/[^']+)'([\s\S]*?)(?=\n  \},)",src):
 im=re.search(r"import\(\s*'\./tools/([^']+)'",m[2])
 if im:routes[im[1].split('/')[-1]]=m[1]
lines=['# PrivKnife application audit — 2026-11-13','','## Verdict','','**Not ready for full functional, bilingual, mobile, or 100% coverage sign-off.** This audit covers every canonical tool in the inventory, running the existing unit suite and browser page-load checks. It is not an exhaustive end-to-end certification: file upload/export round trips, every control, physical phones, Safari, loaded states and all edge cases were not exercised. Those remain explicit acceptance work, not implied passes.','','## Method and evidence','','- Target: http://localhost:4200; installed headless Chromium via Puppeteer, 390×900 touch emulation and 1440×900 desktop, English and Spanish persisted language. This is Chromium, not a physical phone or branded Google Chrome session.','- Browser evidence: [browser.json](audit-evidence/browser.json), including DOM text, document language, ad elements, overflow and page exceptions. Page-load/no-overflow does not prove usability or correct processing.','- Unit baseline: **137 files passed, 1 failed; 1,733 tests passed, 1 failed**. See [baseline log](audit-evidence/tests-no-coverage.log).','- Original coverage command failed because no coverage provider was installed. A temporary `npm install --no-save --package-lock=false @vitest/coverage-v8@4.0.8` enabled collection and resolved Vitest from 4.1.11 to 4.0.8 locally; package manifests/lockfile were not intentionally changed. Results across these environments must not be directly treated as regressions.','- Final coverage uses reportOnFailure and default Angular mapping: [measured log](audit-evidence/coverage-measured.log), [file coverage](audit-evidence/coverage-summary.json). The earlier custom source-glob experiment returned spurious zero coverage and is invalid; do not use coverage-final.log for percentages.','- Build succeeds: [build log](audit-evidence/build.log). Initial bundle total 386.52 kB, estimated transfer 105.53 kB; this includes initial assets, so separately measure initial JS against the repository 200KB requirement.','- Test descriptions per tool: [inventory](audit-evidence/test-inventory.json). Descriptions indicate intended coverage, not proof every assertion is adequate.','','## Prioritized findings','','### High: 100% coverage requirement is unmet','','Measured overall coverage: statements 78.04%, branches 61.70%, functions 49.93%, lines 81.28%. Per-tool measured-file aggregates follow below. Uninstrumented workers/unloaded files may be absent: these numbers are not proof of complete source inclusion. Add a supported coverage provider, include all engines/components/workers, exclude only justified non-executable fixtures/types, and enforce per-file 100% statements/branches/functions/lines in CI. Never count test quantity as coverage.','','### High: advertising divs remain','','Remove ad-slot markup from affected tools (matrix below), including conditional download dialogs and sidebar/leaderboard placeholders. Reproduce by opening the tool and inspecting `[class*="ad-slot"]`. Source examples: invoice-maker.component.ts:62, grid-paper.component.ts:56, barcode-labels.component.ts:59, table-tent-maker.component.ts:56, markdown-cheatsheet.component.ts:57. No evidence here establishes an active advertising network; the confirmed failure is the placeholders themselves.','','### High: tests do not all pass','','- Baseline favicon-generator.component.spec.ts:66 assigns to read-only navigator.clipboard. Fix mocking with a configurable property stub and restore it afterward; verify clipboard success and denial in a real browser. This is a harness failure, not confirmed user-facing breakage.','- Coverage runs also exposed bank-statement-converter.component.spec.ts:136 and :151 clipboard mocking failures and 5-second timeouts in braille-ada-sign-generator/engine.spec.ts:158 and parametric-lamp-designer.component.spec.ts:140. Failures vary by run; see logs. Separate instrumentation/load overhead from actual algorithm performance before changing timeout budgets.','- jsdom reports missing Canvas/WebGL and unimplemented navigation. Passing mocked tests cannot establish visual correctness, actual mesh rendering, or browser downloads.','','### High: privacy architecture needs remediation','','`tools/dev/web-vitals/engine.ts:79` constructs Google PageSpeed requests; its runPageSpeedAudit calls fetch. This is remote processing, incompatible with a blanket local-only tool promise. Mark this tool explicitly external/disabled or remove it from the private suite. DoH may be allowed by the repository exception but must be disclosed and tested separately. No private user data was submitted to these services during this audit.','','### High: bilingual completeness is not established by dictionary parity','','The static dictionaries have 479 English and 479 Spanish keys, with no missing Spanish keys ([comparison](audit-evidence/locales.json)). Rendered text comparisons below identify unchanged English phrases for review; identifiers, units, brands and user content may legitimately remain unchanged. Check validation errors, options, help, tooltips, dialogs, exported documents and screen-reader labels in both languages. Web Vitals validation at component.ts:466 is explicitly hardcoded English. Route title strings are also English in app.routes.ts.','','### Medium: responsive results are only initial-state checks','','No overflow means document scrollWidth did not exceed viewport width at capture. It does not exclude clipped content, tiny targets, overlapping controls, overflowing dialogs or inaccessible canvases. Require 320/360/390/768/1024/1440px, landscape, 200% zoom, keyboard and touch tests with valid/error/processing/result states. For 3D tools test orbit gestures versus page scrolling; for PDF/image tools test selection coordinates at device-pixel ratios 1–3.','','## Per-tool matrix','','S/B/F/L = aggregate percentages over measured files for the tool. “load” means DOM capture completed, not functional certification. Each tool still needs the workflow and edge-case gates below.','','| Tool / route | EN mobile / desktop | ES mobile / desktop | Ad markup in source | S / B / F / L | Existing test cases |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
for x in sorted(inv,key=lambda x:x['tool']):
 route=routes.get(x['tool'],''); rows=[z for z in r if z['route']==route]
 def status(lang,width):
  a=[z for z in rows if z['lang']==lang and z['width']==width]
  if not a:return 'not checked'
  z=a[-1]
  return 'blocked' if z.get('error') else 'overflow' if z.get('overflow') else 'load'
 entries=[v for k,v in cov.items() if '/tools/' in k and '/'+x['tool']+'/' in k]; vals=[]
 for metric in ['statements','branches','functions','lines']:
  t=sum(e[metric]['total'] for e in entries);c=sum(e[metric]['covered'] for e in entries);vals.append(f'{100*c/t:.1f}' if t else 'n/a')
 lines.append(f"| {x['tool']} (`/{route}`) | {status('en',390)} / {status('en',1440)} | {status('es',390)} / {status('es',1440)} | {'**YES**' if x['ad'] else 'not found'} | {' / '.join(vals)} | {len(x['tests'])} |")
lines+=['','## Tool-specific verification backlog','','Each entry lists existing edge-oriented test descriptions (when found) and rendered untranslated-text candidates. These are triage evidence, not a declaration that all other cases pass.']
for x in sorted(inv,key=lambda x:x['tool']):
 route=routes.get(x['tool'],'');rows=[z for z in r if z['route']==route and not z.get('error')];en=next((z for z in rows if z['lang']=='en'),{});es=next((z for z in rows if z['lang']=='es'),{})
 same=sorted(set(en.get('text','').splitlines())&set(es.get('text','').splitlines()));same=[s for s in same if len(s)>25 and re.search('[a-zA-Z]',s)][:5]
 edges=[t for t in x['tests'] if re.search('invalid|empty|error|corrupt|reject|zero|boundary|negative|NaN|limit|unicode|overflow',t,re.I)][:6]
 lines+=['',f"### {x['tool']}",'',f"Source: `{x['path']}`. Route: `/{route}`."]
 lines+=['- Existing edge-oriented tests: '+('; '.join(edges) if edges else 'none identifiable from test descriptions; inspect assertions and add boundary tests')+'.']
 if same:lines+=['- Unchanged rendered EN/ES text to review: '+ '; '.join('`'+s.replace('`','')+'`' for s in same)+'.']
 lines+=['- Required completion: exercise valid input → configure → preview → export → independently reopen/validate output → reset/repeat, in both languages and viewport sizes. Test malformed/empty input, boundary limits, cancellation, repeated operations and resource cleanup.']
lines+=['','## Acceptance gates still required','','1. **Documents:** encrypted/truncated PDFs, rotated pages, page ranges, Unicode fonts, page dimensions, redaction irreversibility via text/image extraction, signatures, print pagination. Independently parse every exported PDF and verify content.','2. **Images/media:** corrupt MIME-disguised files, orientation, alpha, huge dimensions, batch failures, supported HEIC/AVIF codecs, output decoding, metadata removal, before/after pixel and dimension checks.','3. **Audio/video:** zero-length and unsupported codecs, trim bounds, variable frame rate, duration/sync, cancellation, memory limits, >100MB streaming/chunking, independent playback of output.','4. **3D:** minimum/maximum/negative dimensions, empty text, accented Spanish, mesh NaNs, watertightness, dimensions and units, independent STL/3MF parsing, stress performance, worker progress and disposal.','5. **Text/dev/data:** empty/malformed CSV, quotes/newlines, delimiters, Unicode, formula injection, invalid dates/timezones, locale decimal separators, malicious SVG/HTML, known cryptographic vectors and export round trips.','6. **Privacy/security:** real browser request monitoring during processing, sanitize untrusted rendered HTML/SVG, inspect production CSP headers, verify workers and object URLs are released after reset/navigation.','7. **Localization:** change language through the visible selector without reload, persist choice, errors/help/output localization, no raw translation keys, verify long Spanish labels at 320px.','8. **Coverage:** deterministic clean-install CI run; all tools and workers included; all four metrics 100% per file; inspect assertions and boundary partitions because even 100% coverage cannot prove every possible edge case.','','## Reproduction','','From `PrivKnife/`: `npm test -- --watch=false`; `npm run build`. Audit coverage: `npm test -- --watch=false --coverage --runner-config=audit-vitest.config.mjs` after installing a compatible provider. Browser harness: `node audit-run.mjs` (requires localhost:4200 and /usr/bin/chromium). The harness only opens pages; it does not drive full workflows.','']
pathlib.Path('APPLICATION_AUDIT_2026-11-13.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
